      "body": "I know that there a code to encapsule scripts, as hold the load of scripts or header, if cookies are accepted then header/scripts are loaded, if not are accepted scripts never loads. \r\nIf my knowledge in java were not almost null, I would help this and more things, I will try to look for the code to see if it only supposes you do copy and paste or it entails more work.\r\n\r\nI am thinking that the VA administrators can place, manually editing the file, those additional scripts next to the default code that you are going to include with phpvms7, and thus they would fulfill the GDPR by loading or blocking the scripts contained in that fragment according to whether the user accepts or does not accept, Would it work?  Thanks!",
