      "created_at": "2018-09-20T11:06:29Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-20T11:28:54Z",
      "body": "- Opt-in simple: it is the method of registration with a single click confirmation, once entered in the form the email address (among other information).\r\n\r\n- Double opt-in or confirmed opt-in: includes an additional step to confirm the subscription. Once the form has been completed and the request has been sent, click on the confirmation message sent automatically to the new contact. A method to ensure that the email address entered is valid and that the user is the actual owner.\r\n\r\nThe Opt-in must register. Therefore, you should always be able to demonstrate how you have compiled the option so that its legal validity can be proven.\r\n\r\nThis issue GDPR Compliance #244 should be a priority, since all registered users (in beta for example) using forms that do not comply with the GDPR are illegal, and they would have to re-register once the form complies with the GDPR.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
