      "created_at": "2018-09-20T16:19:06Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-09-20T16:27:02Z",
      "body": "> \r\n> \r\n> I'm a little confused about the ask - there already is the double-opt in - they're required to confirm their email address. Do you just want a generic \"opt-in\" checkbox that the VA can use when developing features that involve tracking?\r\n> \r\n> There's going to be an opt-in checkbox anyway for the emails and unsubscribe\r\n> \r\n> I'll add in the callback code for the cookies - good catch\r\n\r\nOnly the described by discord this afternoon, so yes, a future opt-in is that I want to privacy policy and for emails etc.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> \r\n> \r\n> Actually it looks like for the cookies that a notice needs to be set that they're being used. I'm not sure how disabling cookies entirely would work. Is that something you can test? Shutting off cookies, logging in and trying to use the site? You can try it on http://demo.phpvms.net\r\n\r\nGDPR require that no cookie is accepted without consent (explicit consent, same that register form), not only a notice (implied), usually a warning is included in the cookie policy or in the same message indicating that some of them are technically necessary for the web to work. login etc.\r\n\r\n![cookies1](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16170732/45829693-ca33b680-bcfb-11e8-8c94-f6cfa68337ec.JPG)\r\n\r\n![cookies2](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16170732/45829712-d0299780-bcfb-11e8-8da5-910de58ec3c4.JPG)\r\n.\r\n.\r\n.\r\n.\r\n.\r\n.\r\n\r\n![cookies3](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16170732/45831671-43350d00-bd00-11e8-8f86-876a2ed1e44d.JPG)\r\n### **full text of the article from the image above: Here is an explanation about the cookie consent :** https://www.cookiebot.com/en/cookie-consent/\r\n\r\nIt is the general norm, but I am not sure if it always applies to all cookies because sometimes there is a distinction between technical/necessary cookies and others, I think so, because get user personal data to remember preferences, etc (login= ¿user id, email, IP?).\r\n\r\nI leave the link here in case someone needs to consult to make their compliance with GDPR in the future or it could be included in the forum although it is somewhat focused on jimdo.\r\nhttps://jimdo-legal.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360000189886-GDPR\r\n\r\nP.S: I think you only have to worry about the cookies of the phpvms system.\r\nGoogle adsense, G. analytics etc, it should be the work of the owner of the VA, but it would be good to leave a space in which putting the scripts of third parties, in a section of the code that you enable, be blocked or unlocked according to the user accept the cookies or not. It's what I wanted to say in my first message.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
